# Getting started with {data.name}

mdsvex lets you write _markdown_ with *Svelte* in it[^why]. Install it:

```sh
npm install -D mdsvex@next
```

:::tip[Before you start]
You need **Svelte 5**. See the [migration guide](/docs/migrating) for `0.x` projects.
:::

## Options

| option | type | default |
| ------ | ---- | ------- |
| `extensions` | `string[]` | `[".svx"]` |
| `unwrap_images` | `boolean` | `false` |

1. Add the preprocessor to `svelte.config.js`
2. Create a `.svx` file
3. Import it like a component: `import Doc from './doc.svx'`

<Tabs items={["npm", "pnpm"]}>
  {#snippet tab(name)}
    Run `{name} install`.
  {/snippet}
</Tabs>

> Note: `{` and `}` are expressions. Write `\{` for a brace.

[^why]: Because ::youtube[demos](id=abc) are nicer than screenshots.
